From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm relay: TF_GLM_OVN_EXCHANGE_KB, a direct exchange posted in pieces

ai-engine 35b9011e0 applied clean onto the pin stack (one file, cuda_relay.zig). A
direct exchange's send and receive go in pieces of at most EXCHANGE_KB KiB; the
pieces land where the whole would, byte for byte, and NCCL pairs the postings per
peer and kind in order, so each whole send's pieces start where it starts with the
same count. Knob unset (0) posts the whole buffer exactly as before.

The source note: a 4,096-row chunk's 11 MB share gathers at a seventh of the rate a
4 MB one does, which is what the knob addresses. Comment lines single-lined to meet
the lean rule.

Gates on pin+0001..0013: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: every TF_* setting this patch reads is a row of platform/environment.zig with a line in docs/environment.md, read through cuda.ovn or environment, never getenv. Row: TF_GLM_OVN_EXCHANGE_KB (u64, KiB).
- cuda_relay.zig has no commit in 9c9bf542..v1.2.7; applies as is.
- source: work/fold/0017-exchange-kb.patch

